<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Saint Vincent and the Grenadines</h1><p class="st-meta">1979 CE – present · capital Kingstown</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Multi-island state in the Windwards, independent since 1979, shaped by bananas, volcanic eruptions and long-serving prime ministers.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-saint-vincent">Colony of Saint Vincent</a> became independent with the northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grenadines">Grenadines</a> on 27 October 1979 under Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milton-cato">Milton Cato</a>. Weeks later a brief armed uprising on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-island">Union Island</a> was put down with help from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/barbados">Barbados</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/james-mitchell-vincentian-politician">James Mitchell</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-democratic-party-saint-vincent-and-the-grenadines">New Democratic Party</a> governed from 1984 to 2000, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ralph-gonsalves">Ralph Gonsalves</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unity-labour-party">Unity Labour Party</a> from 2001 to 2025. Bananas sustained farmers until European preferences ended, and the economy turned toward tourism, yachting in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grenadines">Grenadines</a> and offshore services. Voters rejected a new constitution that would have made the country a republic in 2009. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argyle-international-airport">Argyle International Airport</a> opened in 2017.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-soufriere-saint-vincent">La Soufrière</a> erupted in April 2021, forcing thousands to evacuate, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hurricane-beryl">Hurricane Beryl</a> devastated the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grenadines">Grenadines</a> in 2024. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-democratic-party-saint-vincent-and-the-grenadines">New Democratic Party</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/godwin-friday">Godwin Friday</a> won the election of November 2025, and the country remains a parliamentary monarchy.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/saint-vincent-and-the-grenadines.jpg" alt="Saint Vincent and the Grenadines" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Saint_Vincent_and_the_Grenadines.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1979 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kingstown</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Milton Cato, James Mitchell, Ralph Gonsalves</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Anglicanism and Methodism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>English and Vincentian Creole</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/saint-vincent-and-the-grenadines">Saint Vincent and the Grenadines</a></dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=2002&amp;focus=saint-vincent-and-the-grenadines" aria-label="Saint Vincent and the Grenadines on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="3001 1688 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Saint Vincent and the Grenadines lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3321 1944L3321 1944"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3321 1944h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3321 1944h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3321 1944h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kingstown. <a href="/atlas?year=2002&amp;focus=saint-vincent-and-the-grenadines">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
